1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
[Original narration] One extremely
hot evening in early July…

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:07,790
This is “Crime and Punishment”,
read by a professional voice.

3
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:11,980
On Audible it costs €18.99.

4
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,700
Here… zero.

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:17,980
And it's not the only one: there
are almost 6,700 more audiobooks,

6
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:22,220
no ads, no subscription, and they
don't even ask for your email.

7
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:23,790
So what's the catch?

8
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,520
We tested it thoroughly: the catalog,

9
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:29,720
the voices, the app,
the best and the worst.

10
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,160
And if you want all the data and sources,

11
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,560
the full review is on our blog:

12
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,380
link in the description.

13
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:39,500
It's called El Libro
Total, and it isn't new:

14
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,660
it was born in Colombia in 2005,

15
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:46,460
run by a non-profit foundation
funded by a software company.

16
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:50,220
Its name is a tribute to
Borges' infinite library.

17
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:55,820
Today it has over 5 million downloads
and a 4.8 rating on Google Play.

18
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:57,580
Let's get to the audiobooks.

19
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:02,860
There are exactly 6,698,
almost all in Spanish.

20
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:08,300
Mind you: most are short stories,
and half are under 18 minutes long.

21
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:10,420
But there are full novels too:

22
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:13,313
“Crime and Punishment” runs over 26 hours,

23
00:01:13,353 --> 00:01:16,060
and “Anna Karenina”, almost 41.

24
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,127
And you can filter them
by more than 700 topics,

25
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:22,190
from mystery to impossible love.

26
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,600
How does it work?

27
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:27,040
You search for “Crime and
Punishment” and the book shows up…

28
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:29,600
but also music inspired by the novel,

29
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,570
illustrations and articles:
everything here is connected.

30
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:36,000
The book page offers several translations,

31
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,810
even the Russian original.

32
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:40,820
You tap “Ir al libro” (Go to
book), then the speaker icon…

33
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:43,180
[Original narration] …a young
man left the tiny room he rented…

34
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,940
…and the text is highlighted while
the pages turn by themselves.

35
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:49,070
You read and listen at the same time.

36
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,420
What about the voices?

37
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:53,500
They're human, from a
small team of narrators:

38
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:57,860
in our sample, Álvaro Gómez Zafra
reads one in three audiobooks,

39
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,500
and this one is by Hernando Iván Cano.

40
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:03,460
However, you can't choose the narrator.

41
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:08,420
The audio is 64 kbps MP3:
good enough for speech,

42
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,580
but far from Audible's studio quality,

43
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:13,200
and the volume varies from book to book.

44
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,000
And here's what nobody else has:

45
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,320
dozens of dictionaries one click away,

46
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:23,200
some of them three centuries old;
side-by-side reading in three languages;

47
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:26,080
and each book's vocabulary: in this one,

48
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:30,450
Raskolnikov appears 972 times.

49
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:33,020
You don't need an account to listen;

50
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:36,060
if you sign up, for free, you get history,

51
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:37,700
favorites and notes.

52
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:39,900
On mobile you get speed control,

53
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:43,060
up to 2x, which doesn't exist on desktop.

54
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:46,100
But watch out: offline, you can only read.

55
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,160
The audio needs an internet connection.

56
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:51,760
The best: it's truly free, with no ads,

57
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,320
human voices and synchronized text,

58
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,720
something almost no one offers.

59
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:59,680
The worst: no new releases or bestsellers,

60
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,760
only classics and donated
works; the player is basic,

61
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:09,090
no sleep timer or downloads; and
the website is slow and a bit dated.

62
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,580
Who is it for?

63
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:14,980
Students, lovers of the
classics and language learners.

64
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,980
If you're after the latest
thriller, this isn't for you.

65
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:24,060
And the savings are real: this same
audiobook costs €15 to €19 in stores.

66
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,480
Here, zero.

67
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,600
The catch?

68
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,530
There isn't one.

69
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:30,800
Our score: 8.2 out of 10.

70
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,520
And to find out where to
listen to any audiobook,

71
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,640
and at what price,
search for it on SonorBooks.

72
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:39,450
Your next story is waiting for you.
